# HakiOS defconfig for the POCO C75 4G / Redmi 14C (lake, MediaTek MT6768 / Helio G81 Ultra):
# the common kernel's configuration, the MT6768's facts and drivers
# (mtk/mt6768/configs/mt6768.config in the common repository, which leaves every Qualcomm driver
# out), and this phone's own fragment. What tools/xnu-cycle.sh and .github/workflows/build.yml run:
# make lake_defconfig && make kernel, then the kernel into boot_a through mtkloader.
#
# common_defconfig and mt6768.config belong to the shared kernel tree. tools/mkconfig.py looks for
# them next to this file, then in $HAKIOS_KERNEL_TREE (or $HAKIOS_CONFIG_DIR), and names the ones it
# could not find; a device-only configuration still comes out, which is enough for mtkloader.
#include common_defconfig
#include mt6768.config
#include lake.config
